+     * room's info card; in a DM, Element's user info of the other member), `members`, `files`, `pinned` or `search` (Element's own message search: the field and the results, RoomView's search path). Replaces an open
+     * panel or thread panel. `done` (`roomId`) when it closes: its close button, Escape, a later open, `closePanel`, the room
+     * left, another room opened from it, the bridge disposed. `unknown_room` as the other actions; `unsupported` for a room the user has not joined, and a DM whose other member is unknown. The card's own writes
+     * (favourite, leave, invite, unpin ...) are Element's. Awaits a right-panel view-model.
+     */
+    openPanel(roomId: string, card: "info" | "members" | "files" | "pinned" | "search"): Promise<ActionOutcome>;
+    /**
+     * M14 K4 (version 8, additive: a kit feature-checks it): Element's own user info of `userId` in the host panel slot, the
+     * right-panel `MemberInfo` card of a member of `roomId` (the MXID, and under it the DID row). A sender's name or avatar in
+     * the kit opens it. Same slot and lifecycle as `openPanel`: replaces an open panel or thread, `done` (`roomId`) when it
+     * closes (its close button, Escape, a later open, `closePanel`, the room left, another room opened from it, the bridge
+     * disposed). `unknown_room` as `openPanel`; `unsupported` for a room not joined, an empty user id, or a user the room has
+     * no member object for. The card's own writes (invite, ignore, power level ...) are Element's. Awaits a right-panel view-model.
+     */
+    openUserInfo(roomId: string, userId: string): Promise<ActionOutcome>;
+    /**
+     * M14 K6 (additive, version stays 8): copies the Markdown of a message to the clipboard through Element's own
+     * `eventToMarkdown` and `copyPlainTextToClipboard` (the registry patch's "Copy Markdown" action), in the same call
+     * stack as the click (the clipboard needs the user gesture). `done` (`roomId`, `eventId`) when the clipboard took it;
+     * `unknown_room` / `unknown_event` as the other message actions; `unsupported` where `canCopyMarkdown` is not set;
+     * `failed` when the clipboard refused the text. Changes nothing else.
+     */
+    copyMarkdown(roomId: string, eventId: string): Promise<ActionOutcome>;
+    /** M9: closes whatever the host panel slot shows (a card panel or a thread panel); a no-op when it is empty. */
+    closePanel(): void;
+    /** M9: Element asked, from a card panel, to show an event of the panel's room (a Pinned "View in timeline", a file's jump). */
+    onJump(cb: (jump: { roomId: string; eventId: string }) => void): () => void;
+    /** M9: Element asked, from a card panel, to show another room (a "Message" from user info); the panel is closed. */
+    onRoomOpen(cb: (open: { roomId: string; eventId?: string }) => void): () => void;
+    /**
+     * M7 E4: Element's own report dialog over the kit (`Action.OpenReportEventDialog`, as the message context menu opens
+     * it). `done` when the dialog closes (a report sent, cancelled or dismissed alike: Element shows the result itself,
+     * the kit keeps no state), `forbidden` for an own message (Element offers Report only on others'), `unknown_room` /
+     * `unknown_event` for a message the bridge does not hold. Interim (D31): no report action on a shared view-model.
+     */
+    openReport(roomId: string, eventId: string): Promise<ActionOutcome>;
+    /**
+     * M10 W4 (additive, kit feature-checks it): Element's own settings dialog on its Account tab over the kit
+     * (`Action.ViewUserSettings`, `UserTab.Account`: name and avatar are `UserProfileSettings`; Element's other tabs show
+     * too, D17). `done` when the dialog closes (Element saves the profile itself; the kit follows `me()`), `failed` when
+     * the dialog does not open, another Element dialog action is running, or the session is a guest's (Element would
